    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20306" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hĕbĕtesco</span></b> ,
			ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [hebes], <i>to
				grow dull</i>, <i>dim</i>, or <i>faint</i> (post-Aug. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aciem in cultris tonsorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 7, 23, § 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acies oculi hebetescit ac paene caligat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 6, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolor hebetescit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 56</span></i>
			.</div>
